  "body": "Keyboard users could not identify campaign status controls, and the sticky page header completely hid focused status/notes fields at320px and1280px. Label the visible MUI selects with their row and column, name the campaign progress indicators, and keep the shared page heading in document flow. Also name eight loading indicators confirmed during the remaining initial role audit. Resolves A11Y-01, extends UX-260917-023 and fixes confirmed UX-260917-032.\n\nValidation: production TypeScript/build365423gzip with5preloads; affected lint;14 slow-response ES/EN cases;10 browser cases across5profiles and3engines, each checking all5campaign tabs, row/column names, keyboard menus, visible focus, axe and reflow. Before/after screenshots and actual isolated API evidence included. Records19 additional completed role fixtures/3762 arrivals, with untested actions/states/native explicitly retained; navigation500 is isolated in #432. Updates #429 actual merge/Cloudflare/synthetic production smoke and store review evidence. No campaigns, messages, budgets or real payment operations submitted; no field-performance or human screen-reader claim.\n\n\n\nLatest head dabb773a2 includes main2f01 and explicit nearest scrolling for focused campaign controls. Linux CI on prior e91 exposed a partially clipped notes input after Select dismissal; screenshot retained and regression unchanged. Final local production bundle365447gzip/5preloads, TypeScript and lint pass. Nine final browser cases passed; Firefox1280 timed out during axe under simulator pressure, then passed unchanged after shutting down the owned simulator. Earlier pre-portal-guard ten cases passed. Current hosted Linux run remains required. All23 remaining role fixtures completed4554 arrivals, covering31 derived roles together with prior evidence; dynamic actions, all state combinations and human screen readers are not implied. Native UX033 is recorded separately in mobile PR101.\n",
